// Pull request author: KKarishan
// Change: new rule
// Title: Hidden Local User Account Creation Attempt Via Net.EXE
// Sigma ID: 8106cdf0-7503-49a9-806a-c5cee9885369
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Keshon Karishan (KKarishan)
// Date: 2026-08-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1136.001
// Description: Detects the attempt to create a hidden local user account via the Windows Net.EXE utility by
//   appending a dollar sign ($) to the username. The dollar sign at the end of the username hides
//   the account from the Windows login screen and other user interfaces. Threat actors may use this
//   technique to create hidden accounts for persistence stealthily, allowing them to maintain access
//   to a compromised system without being easily detected.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/@toon.commander/hidden-windows-accounts-a-stealth-technique-abused-by-attackers-6f7e0b0f7063
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/4dd00b24e0b32f6154064f1313ecea11beaef50e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_net_user_hidden_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\net.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\net1.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("net.exe", "net1.exe"))) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "user" and ProcessCommandLine contains "add" and ProcessCommandLine contains "$")
